# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Generated installable skill artifact (built on demand from the package)
*.skill
dist/

# Local context / internal notes — never publish (source tickets, plans, etc.)
control/

# This project uses its own skill. A `.handoff/` config binds a checkout to one
# machine's install and points at that checkout's local notes, so it is per-clone
# state, not shared source — the same reasoning as `.claude/*` below, and it holds
# for any contributor who adopts the skill, not just the maintainer. The handoff
# file itself lives under `control/`, already excluded above.
.handoff/

# The agent harness's own folder defaults to OUT, and a clone's share is named
# in. Nothing here is written by this project: the harness creates files on its
# own schedule, and what it stores includes directory sources resolved to
# absolute machine paths. Until this rule existed, .claude/settings.local.json
# was excluded only by the maintainer's *global* gitignore — real protection on
# one machine and none for any contributor, and invisible from inside the repo
# because a clean `git status` is what both cases look like.
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: an excluded directory cannot have its
# contents re-included, so the exception below needs the contents excluded.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
